  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Exact provider selection",
      "items": [
        "Groq is selected when its key exists, unless a Gemini key and a GEMINI_MODEL beginning gemini- select Gemini.",
        "Groq tries the configured model, then coded alternatives on HTTP 404. Gemini uses its configured model and JSON schema format.",
        "Chat streaming, source search, transcription and speech have separate call paths; they do not inherit every retry rule shown here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Trust and concurrency",
      "items": [
        "Source text, learner answers and preferences are untrusted data. Server-side validators still enforce structure and domain rules.",
        "Per-session locks and compare-and-update revisions protect study mutations within one API process. Model calls share a three-slot semaphore.",
        "Owner quota is charged per generate call; deployment quota is charged per outer attempt. Domain-level course/feedback correction is separate from transient retries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reading continuation boxes",
      "items": [
        "A box tagged Continue repeats an existing named step. It represents a return or handoff to that step, not a new service or a separate task.",
        "The vertical path shows one successful route; labeled branches preserve the other conditions and recovery actions."
      ]
    }
  ]
